README.md:53:My goal this year was to make something "fun", relatively easy (at least for the first few levels), and something with a more global appeal. I took a lot of inspiration from 3d Mario and Zelda games.
README.md:75:For tools, I continued with [Google Closure Compiler](https://github.com/google/closure-compiler), but the major breakthrough tool was [Roadroller](https://lifthrasiir.github.io/roadroller/) by [Kang Seonghoon](https://mearie.org/). In the past, I had looked at [RegPack](https://siorki.github.io/regPack.html), but it couldn't handle 20kb input. Kang Seonghoon created the industrial strength version of RegPack, which is perfect for js13k. The tool was released in the middle of the competition, and it was essentially a gift of roughly 5kb additional space. In the end, this project was not size constrained at all.
README.md:83:* The non-gameplay features such as the opening scene, after-level cutscene, and end-of-game cutscene were all praised.
README.md:88:* I still have a tendency to add features rather than exploring fun or novel gameplay. The level design was simplistic, primarily because I didn't spend enough time on it.
README.md:90:* The jetpack mechanic was fun, but landing was difficult due to depth issues. This was not game breaking, but it added cognitive load.
